- content_for :og_image, asset_url('baldrick-buddy-screenshot.png')

= render 'shared/fun_stuff_page', page_title: 'Baldrick Buddy', current_page: 'Baldrick Buddy', page_subtitle: 'Find Baldrick boards on your network and update their firmware', document_title: 'Baldrick Buddy - Fun Stuff', meta: ['Mac, Windows & Linux', 'Network scanner', 'Firmware updates'], toc: baldrick_buddy_toc do
  p.lead Baldrick Buddy is a desktop app that scans your local network for Baldrick boards, shows their status at a glance, and makes firmware updates a one-click affair.

  .prose
    section#overview
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Overview
        | What is Baldrick Buddy?

      p Instead of hunting for board IP addresses or opening each web interface in turn, Baldrick Buddy discovers your boards automatically and lists them in one place; board name, type, firmware version, IP address, and uptime.

      figure.figure
        .fimg
          = image_tag 'baldrick-buddy-screenshot.png', alt: 'Baldrick Buddy showing two boards on the network with firmware update option'

      p When a newer firmware is available, Buddy shows an update button right in the list. Hit Rescan any time you've powered on a new board or changed networks.

    section#download
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Download
        | Get Baldrick Buddy

      - if @release
        - mac_asset = @release.asset_for('mac')
        - windows_asset = @release.asset_for('windows')
        - linux_asset = @release.asset_for('linux')
        .buddy-downloads data-controller="buddy-download" data-buddy-download-mac-url-value=(mac_asset ? baldrick_buddy_download_path(asset_id: mac_asset.id, locale: nil) : '') data-buddy-download-windows-url-value=(windows_asset ? baldrick_buddy_download_path(asset_id: windows_asset.id, locale: nil) : '') data-buddy-download-linux-url-value=(linux_asset ? baldrick_buddy_download_path(asset_id: linux_asset.id, locale: nil) : '') data-buddy-download-version-value=@release.tag_name
          .buddy-primary
            a.btn.btn-solid.buddy-primary-btn href="#download" data-buddy-download-target="primary"
              span.buddy-primary-label data-buddy-download-target="label" Download Baldrick Buddy
              span.ar ↓
            .buddy-primary-meta
              p.buddy-primary-hint data-buddy-download-target="hint" Detecting your platform…
              p.buddy-version
                | Latest:
                strong= " #{@release.tag_name}"
                - if @release.published_at
                  span= " · #{l(@release.published_at.to_date, format: :long)}"

          .buddy-download-grid
            - baldrick_buddy_platforms.each do |platform|
              - asset = @release.asset_for(platform[:id])
              .buddy-download-card id="download-#{platform[:id]}" data-buddy-download-target="card" data-platform=platform[:id] class=(asset ? nil : 'is-unavailable')
                .buddy-card-icon
                  = baldrick_buddy_platform_icon(platform[:id])
                .buddy-card-body
                  h3= platform[:label]
                  - if asset
                    p.buddy-filename= asset.name
                    p.buddy-size= number_to_human_size(asset.size)
                  - else
                    p.buddy-unavailable No build for this release yet.
                - if asset
                  = link_to baldrick_buddy_download_path(asset_id: asset.id, locale: nil), class: 'btn btn-line-light btn-sm buddy-card-btn' do
                    | Download
                    span.ar ↓
                - else
                  span.buddy-card-btn.is-disabled Unavailable
      - else
        .callout.warn
          span.ic
            svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
              path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"
              path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01"
          div
            span.lbl Downloads temporarily unavailable
            p.bd We're having trouble fetching the latest release. Please try again shortly or #{link_to 'contact support', support_path}.

      p.small Baldrick Buddy is not code-signed. You'll need to approve it once on first launch — see the platform notes below.

    section#macos
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot macOS
        | Installing on Mac

      p On first launch, macOS Gatekeeper may block the app because it isn't signed with an Apple Developer certificate.

      ol
        li Download and open the <code>.dmg</code> file.
        li Drag Baldrick Buddy to Applications.
        li <strong>Right-click</strong> the app in Applications and choose <strong>Open</strong> (don't double-click the first time).
        li Click <strong>Open</strong> in the dialog to confirm.
      p Alternatively, go to <strong>System Settings → Privacy & Security</strong> and click <strong>Open Anyway</strong> after the first blocked launch. You only need to do this once.

    section#windows
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Windows
        | Installing on Windows

      p Windows SmartScreen may warn that Baldrick Buddy is from an unknown publisher. This is expected for unsigned software.

      ol
        li Download and run the installer or <code>.exe</code>.
        li When SmartScreen appears, click <strong>More info</strong>.
        li Click <strong>Run anyway</strong>.
      p If the file was blocked before you ran it, right-click the downloaded file → <strong>Properties</strong> → check <strong>Unblock</strong> at the bottom of the General tab → Apply.

    section#linux
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Linux
        | Installing on Linux

      p Linux builds are distributed as an AppImage (or similar). The app is not signed with a distribution key.

      ol
        li Download the AppImage (or package).
        li Make it executable: <code>chmod +x Baldrick-Buddy-*.AppImage</code>
        li Run it: <code>./Baldrick-Buddy-*.AppImage</code>
      p Some desktop environments show an "untrusted application" prompt — confirm to run. If your distro blocks unknown binaries entirely, run from a terminal so you can see any policy errors.

    section#using-buddy
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Guide
        | Using Baldrick Buddy

      ol
        li Install and launch Baldrick Buddy.
        li Make sure your computer is on the same network as your Baldrick boards.
        li Click <strong>Rescan</strong> if boards don't appear immediately.
        li Click a board's IP to copy it, or use the firmware update button when an update is available.

    section#support
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Help
        | Support

      p Having trouble with Baldrick Buddy or a firmware update? Our support team and community can help.

      .next-grid
        = link_to support_path, class: 'next-card' do
          .top
            span.kind Support
            span.go →
          h4 Need help?
          p Questions about Buddy, updates, or board setup.
        = link_to fun_stuff_baldrick_buddy_privacy_path, class: 'next-card' do
          .top
            span.kind Legal
            span.go →
          h4 Privacy Policy
          p How Buddy handles information on your device and network.
        = link_to t('facebook_group_url'), class: 'next-card', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener' do
          .top
            span.kind Community
            span.go →
          h4 Facebook group
          p Discuss Buddy and share tips with other builders.

section.cta
  .wrap
    h2 Keep your boards current
    p Firmware updates also ship through each board's web interface — check System when your board nudges you.
    .cta-btns
      = link_to fun_stuff_release_notes_path, class: 'btn btn-bone' do
        | Release notes
        span.ar →
      = link_to fun_stuff_path, class: 'btn btn-clear' do
        | All fun stuff
